    "body": "### Problem\n\n# Observations\n\nUsing nvim-lspconfig with basedpyright, vim.lsp sends \"textDocument/didClose\", even though buffer is not closing.\n\n# ~/.local/state/nvim-debug/lsp.log\n\n```\n...\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:48] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"server_request: callback result\"\t{ result = vim.NIL, status = true }\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:48] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"rpc.send\"\t{ id = 6, jsonrpc = \"2.0\", result = vim.NIL }\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:48] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"rpc.receive\"\t{ jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"$/progress\", params = { token = \"949d67ab-632c-43d9-a6ac-4aa88344e7c8\", value = { kind = \"begin\", title = \"\" } } }\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:48] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"rpc.receive\"\t{ jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"$/progress\", params = { token = \"949d67ab-632c-43d9-a6ac-4aa88344e7c8\", value = { kind = \"report\", message = \"1 file to analyze\" } } }\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:48] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"rpc.receive\"\t{ jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"$/progress\", params = { token = \"949d67ab-632c-43d9-a6ac-4aa88344e7c8\", value = { kind = \"end\" } } }\n[DEBUG][2026-09-18 12:38:51] ...r/neovim/0.12.5_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/log.lua:150\t\"rpc.send\"\t{ jsonrpc = \"2.0\", method = \"textDocument/didClose\", params = { textDocument = { uri = \"file:///private/tmp/minimal-python/src/minimal_python/__init__.py\" } } }\n```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\nUse the below minimal `init.lua` together with [this minimal python repo](https://github.com/Chris927/nvim-didClose-issue-minimal-reproduction). When opening `./src/minimal_python/__init__.py` you will first see warning markers (`W`) (see screenshot below), then a stacktrace is printed and warning markers disappear.\n\n```lua\n-- [Chris 2026-09-16] Copied using :read $VIMRUNTIME/example_init.lua, then\n-- stripped down to reproduce didClose issue\n\n-- Install third-party plugins via \"vim.pack.add()\".\nvim.pack.add({\n  'https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig',\n})\n\nvim.lsp.config('basedpyright', {\n    single_file_support = false,\n    settings = {\n        basedpyright = {\n            openFilesOnly = false,\n            analysis = {\n                -- useLibraryCodeForTypes = false,\n                diagnosticMode = \"openFilesOnly\",\n            }\n        }\n    }\n})\n\nvim.lsp.enable('basedpyright')\nvim.lsp.enable('bashls')\n\nvim.lsp.log.set_level(\"debug\")\n\n-- the below produces the stacktrace as per the screenshot, you\n-- can remove it, the same behavior (losing the lsp connection) can\n-- still be observed.\nlocal original_start = vim.lsp.start\nvim.lsp.start = function(config, opts)\n  local client_id = original_start(config, opts)\n  if client_id then\n    local client = vim.lsp.get_client_by_id(client_id)\n    if client and client.rpc and client.rpc.notify then\n      local original_rpc_notify = client.rpc.notify\n      client.rpc.notify = function(method, params)\n        if method == \"textDocument/didClose\" then\n          print(\"[LSP TRACE] rpc.notify didClose for: \" .. vim.inspect(params.textDocument.uri))\n          print(debug.traceback()) -- This will pinpoint the exact file/plugin calling it\n        end\n        return original_rpc_notify(method, params)\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  return client_id\nend\n```\n\n<img width=\"935\" height=\"289\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6a61f1a-2285-42cd-b6f6-b5e8f1f8cee9\" />\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo \"textDocument/didClose\" must be sent, unless buffer(s) for this file are all actually closed or closing.\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.5\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nbasedpyright 1.40.1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacos\n\n### Log file\n\nhttps://gist.github.com/Chris927/c82c7e64a98a3fc405ff92b14f76ecc5",
